{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"title","type":"text","text":"# 🔌 Obsidian Setup\n\n**11 plugins + 2 CSS snippets + GitHub Theme.** The lean stack that turns vanilla Obsidian into the AI OS interface. Read [[04-obsidian-setup|the guide]] for the prose enumeration + fresh-install checklist.","x":-100,"y":-200,"width":900,"height":140,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"doctrine","type":"text","text":"### 📜 Doctrine & metadata layer\n\nFrontmatter, queries, templates — the stuff that makes the markdown act like a database.\n\n- **Templater** — Advanced templating. Powers every note from `04 - Templates/`.\n- **Meta Bind** — Interactive inline inputs + buttons.\n- **Dataview** — Query notes as a database. **Non-negotiable** — half the doctrine is Dataview queries.\n- **Folder Notes** — Notion-style folder-index notes. Each tier folder has a README that feels like the folder itself.\n- **Iconize** — Icons for files/folders/text. Visual scan anchor pairing with the CSS snippets.","x":-450,"y":50,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"visual","type":"text","text":"### 🎨 Visual surfaces\n\nNon-text content inside the vault — drawings, boards, embeds, calendars.\n\n- **Excalidraw** — Sketch tool. Files are markdown + embedded JSON (text-only). The capture surface in `21 - Excalidraw/`. Powers Stage 1 of [[02-brainstorm-to-project]].\n- **Base Board** — Kanban from frontmatter. Cards = notes; columns = property values.\n- **Custom Frames** — Web apps as iframe panes (Google Keep, Todoist presets).\n- **Google Calendar** — Two-way calendar sync. Today's events inline in the daily note.","x":-10,"y":50,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"terminal","type":"text","text":"### ⌨️ Terminal & code\n\nThe bridge from vault to PowerShell.\n\n- **Open in Terminal** — Right-click any folder → opens external PowerShell at that path. Enables running `22 - Scripts/` directly from sidebar context.\n- **oterm** — Full terminal emulator inside Obsidian via xterm.js. PowerShell, WSL, zsh, tmux. Heavier than Open in Terminal but no context switch.","x":430,"y":50,"width":420,"height":380,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"styling","type":"text","text":"### 🎨 Styling\n\n**Theme:** GitHub Theme (clean, code-friendly).\n\n**CSS Snippets (both enabled):**\n\n- **`Colored Sidebar Items`** (CyanVoxel v2.0.0) — Base snippet. Numbered prefix → color. Defaults: 00→mint, 01→cyan, 02→light-blue, 03→blue, 04→violet, 99→cool-gray.\n- **`Tier Extensions`** (Andy's extension) — Adds Tier 2 (reference): 10-14 = red→orange→amber→gold. Tier 2 (output): 20-21 = yellow/lime. Reuses base color variables + adds `--gold`.","x":-450,"y":470,"width":620,"height":340,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"non-included","type":"text","text":"### 🚫 Intentionally NOT installed\n\nThe stack is lean. Plugins skipped:\n\n- **Calendar (date picker)** — Daily Notes filenames are ISO-dated; the Files sidebar sorts correctly without a calendar widget.\n- **Tasks** — Andy's task model is light (top-3 + anti-todo in the daily note); a full task plugin would be overkill.\n- **Kanban (popular one)** — Base Board does the same job from frontmatter, integrating with Dataview.\n- **Many \"must-install\" plugins** — each adds maintenance + drift potential. Bar: \"does this earn its place in CLAUDE.md or a workflow?\"\n\nReassess yearly.","x":195,"y":470,"width":620,"height":340,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"checklist","type":"text","text":"### ✅ Fresh-install checklist\n\n1. Install Obsidian from obsidian.md\n2. Open vault → trust it\n3. Settings → Community plugins → toggle off Restricted mode\n4. Install all 11 plugins from the manifest\n5. Settings → Appearance → install **GitHub Theme**\n6. Settings → Appearance → CSS snippets → toggle on `Colored Sidebar Items` + `Tier Extensions`\n\n**Order matters:** Dataview before opening Dataview-heavy folders. Excalidraw before opening `21 - Excalidraw/` files. Otherwise you'll see plugin-not-loaded errors briefly.","x":-100,"y":850,"width":820,"height":280,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"link-guide","type":"file","file":"14 - How To/guides/04-obsidian-setup.md","x":-100,"y":1170,"width":820,"height":200},
		{"id":"link-vault-index","type":"file","file":"14 - How To/guides/03-vault-index.md","x":-450,"y":1410,"width":420,"height":180},
